# SIDD-Medium — Team Progress Review (29 October 2026)

## Completed Work

- Acquired and verified SIDD-Medium sRGB: 160 scene-instance folders and 320 noisy/ground-truth pairs.
- Prepared a small test dataset of three distinct physical scenes.
- Executed CPU smoke tests of U-Net and NAFNet using two training steps per model.
- Saved model checkpoints, configurations and experimental records.
- Generated visual comparisons and preliminary PSNR measurements.

## Experimental Setup

- Dataset: SIDD-Medium sRGB
- Test subset: 1 training pair, 1 validation pair, 1 test pair
- Inference crop: 64 × 64 pixels
- Models: U-Net and NAFNet
- Training: 2 steps each, batch size 1, CPU

## Important Limitations

**These results demonstrate pipeline functionality, not successful denoising or reproduced benchmark performance.**

Both models currently perform worse than the original noisy images on the measured validation and test crops. The models require substantially more training before meaningful architecture comparisons can be made.

## Next Milestone

Train both baseline models using the complete dataset under a consistent experimental protocol, evaluate PSNR/SSIM, and investigate potential improvements to NAFNet's gating mechanism.

